<!--
    The reference's item-SLOT button templates: `PaperDollItemSlotButtonTemplate` (PaperDollFrame.xml
    l.4-38) and `BagSlotButtonTemplate` (MainMenuBarBagButtons.xml l.17-53), which inherits it. Both
    sit on `ItemButtonTemplate` (ItemButtonTemplate.xml), so the chain is

        ItemButtonTemplate <- PaperDollItemSlotButtonTemplate <- BagSlotButtonTemplate

    and all three are now declared, in that order, across three files the toc loads in that order.

    **Why they are here rather than in CharacterFrame.xml and BagFrame.xml, where their subjects
    live.** Load order, and only load order: BagFrame.xml (toc l.241) comes BEFORE
    CharacterFrame.xml (l.256), so a bag template declared in the former could not inherit a doll
    template declared in the latter. Neither is consumed by our own windows — our doll slots and our
    four bag-bar slots are hand-wired to `BenillaPaperDollSlot_*` / `BenillaBagBarSlot_*` and do not
    inherit these — so a file of their own, loaded after both, costs nothing and makes the chain
    readable. This is the reference's published surface for ADDONS, kept where its dependencies are
    satisfied.

    **The handlers are the reference's own, not transcriptions.** `PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnLoad`,
    `_OnEvent`, `_OnClick`, `_Update`, `_UpdateLock`, `_OnEnter` and `_OnUpdate` come from
    `PaperDollFrame.lua`, which `ui_script::reference_ui` now SOURCES off the player's own patch
    chain. That file earned its place because every one of those acts on `this` and `this:GetID()`
    through live APIs and never on a named reference window — see the note beside SOURCED for what
    was checked first, including the 18 collisions that order settles in our favour.

    `MainMenuBarBagButtons.lua` is deliberately NOT sourced, which is why `BagSlotButton_OnClick`,
    `_OnDrag`, `_OnShiftClick` and `_OnEnter` are ours in BagFrame.xml: all four of its versions walk
    `ContainerFrame1..NUM_CONTAINER_FRAMES`, windows this client does not build, and two of them
    call verbs (`PutItemInBag`, `PickupBagFromSlot`) it does not bind. Sourcing it would have handed
    every caller a body that raises inside the addon's own click wrapper.

    **pfUI is the measured caller**, and it fits the reference's contract exactly rather than by
    luck: it names its bag-bar buttons `pfUIBagsBBag0Slot`.. with a NINE-character prefix, so the
    reference's own `strsub(name, 10)` in `PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnLoad` yields `Bag0Slot` and
    `GetInventorySlotInfo` answers slot 20. It then reads `$parentIconTexture`, `$parentNormalTexture`,
    `GetHighlightTexture()` and `GetPushedTexture()` off what it built, and CHAINS the template's
    OnEnter/OnLeave rather than replacing them (modules/bags.lua l.513-585).

    OUT, named rather than stubbed (1134 §4): the bank arm. `BankItemButtonBagTemplate` and
    `BankItemButtonGenericTemplate` inherit `BankItemButtonTemplate`, whose handlers live in
    `BankFrame.lua` — not sourced — and whose OnEnter calls `this:GetInventorySlot()`, a widget
    method we do not bind. pfUI reaches those only for its bank window.
-->
<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/">
    <!-- Ref PaperDollFrame.xml l.4-38, structure and scripts verbatim. The `$parentCooldown` Model
         is not optional decoration: the sourced `PaperDollItemSlotButton_Update` resolves it by
         name (`getglobal(this:GetName().."Cooldown")`) and calls `:Hide()` / CooldownFrame_SetTimer
         on it every repaint, so a button without one raises on its first update. -->
    <Button name="PaperDollItemSlotButtonTemplate" inherits="ItemButtonTemplate" virtual="true">
        <Frames>
            <Model name="$parentCooldown" inherits="CooldownFrameTemplate"/>
        </Frames>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnLoad();</OnLoad>
            <OnEvent>PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnEvent(event);</OnEvent>
            <OnClick>PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnClick(arg1);</OnClick>
            <OnShow></OnShow>
            <OnDragStart>PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnClick("LeftButton", 1);</OnDragStart>
            <OnReceiveDrag>PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnClick("LeftButton", 1);</OnReceiveDrag>
            <OnEnter>PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnEnter();</OnEnter>
            <OnLeave>
                this.updateTooltip = nil;
                GameTooltip:Hide();
                ResetCursor();
            </OnLeave>
            <OnUpdate>PaperDollItemSlotButton_OnUpdate(arg1);</OnUpdate>
        </Scripts>
    </Button>

    <!-- `BagSlotButtonTemplate` was declared here, transcribed from MainMenuBarBagButtons.xml
         because that file could not be sourced. It IS sourced now — benilla.toc entry 48, one line
         below this file — so the reference's own declaration is the live one and the copy is gone
         (decision 1751, window 3). pfUI and anything else that inherits the template now inherits
         the reference's, including the `$parentItemAnim` Model our copy structurally could not
         carry. -->
</Ui>
